      "content": "That makes sense for the ESG report. But some of the risk management guys are pushing back. They're saying that focusing on outcome instead of just focusing on individual creditworthiness/opportunity might actually introduce bias or make the model less accurate for predicting defaults. How would you address their concern that this approach might compromise the mathematical integrity of the scoring?",
